# L §2.5 (round 14): LOAD-KEY "for a literal where the range's ends and step are literals, which load sees; otherwise
# RUN-KEY where the key is read, and a fulfils or a same side at a key the range doesn't hold names an instance that
# doesn't exist, RUN-RECORD". pay is keyed by 1 .. cnt (cnt a row, 3): pay[5] names no instance, so the observation
# that fulfils it is refused (L §5.19 RUN-RECORD), and the balance that books it. (Writer 6's whole-model LOAD-KEY at
# run is not adopted, round 14's U-8.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input cnt: int
input first_day: date
input bank: observed

move pay[n in 1 .. cnt]: transfers
  on add_days(first_day, n)
  leg cash from konto to world amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "s"
  cnt = 3 "s"
  first_day = 2026-01-01 "s"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-01
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-01-03, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 12.00 PLN, fulfils: pay[5]) "l1"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-RECORD observation bank[r1] fulfils pay[5], which doesn't exist ...
...
